<section id="introduction" class="level1">
<h1>Introduction</h1>
<p>wave~reader is a simple agentic web application designed to well informed beach descriptions, surf forecast and daily surf report to a user by leveraging AI-powered analysis and real-time meteorological data. Built with a sophisticated multi-agent architecture, the application synthesizes wave data, wind patterns, and geographic information to deliver actionable insights for surfers.</p>
<section id="project-vision" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="project-vision">Project Vision</h2>
<p>The core vision of wave~reader is to democratize access to professional-grade surf forecasting through an intuitive, accessible interface. Rather than requiring users to interpret raw meteorological data or consult multiple sources, the application presents curated, AI-generated forecasts that consider complex interactions between ocean conditions, wind patterns, and geographic factors.</p>
<p>This current implementation is only a proof of concept, I am planning on building out more rigid features into the website with the hope of hosting and maintaining it when I feel it is ready.</p>
</section>
<section id="key-features" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="key-features">Key Features</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Multi-Agent Architecture</strong>: Four specialized agents working in concert</li>
<li><strong>Real-Time Data Integration</strong>: Live marine and weather data from Open-Meteo</li>
<li><strong>AI-Generated Forecasts</strong>: GPT-4o-mini powered analysis and predictions</li>
<li><strong>Interactive Visualizations</strong>: Charts and geographic maps for data exploration</li>
<li><strong>Minimal Frontend</strong>: Pure HTML/CSS/JavaScript with no build tools required</li>
<li><strong>Lofi Aesthetic</strong>: Thoughtfully designed user interface with earthy color palette</li>
</ul>
<hr>
</section>
</section>
<section id="architecture-overview" class="level1">
<h1>Architecture Overview</h1>
<section id="system-design" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="system-design">System Design</h2>
<p>wave~reader employs a modular, agent-based architecture that separates concerns and allows for independent scaling of components:</p>
<pre><code>┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    User Interface (Frontend)                │
│         HTML/CSS/JavaScript • Lofi Aesthetic Design          │
└────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │
┌────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  FastAPI Backend (ASGI)                     │
│              Async Request Handling &amp; Routing               │
└────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │
┌────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│              LangGraph Multi-Agent Orchestrator             │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Agent 1: Description Generator (Geolocation &amp; Context)  │
│  │ Agent 2: Coordinate Resolver (Beach Geolocation)        │
│  │ Agent 3: Weather Data Fetcher (Marine &amp; Weather APIs)   │
│  │ Agent 4: Forecast Synthesizer (AI Analysis)             │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │
        ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
        │                                 │
┌───────▼──────────────┐    ┌────────────▼────────────┐
│  Open-Meteo Marine   │    │  Open-Meteo Weather     │
│  API (Swell Data)    │    │  API (Wind Data)        │
└──────────────────────┘    └─────────────────────────┘</code></pre>
</section>
<section id="technology-stack" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="technology-stack">Technology Stack</h2>
<section id="backend" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="backend">Backend</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Python 3.14</strong> with <code>uv</code> package manager for fast, deterministic dependency management</li>
<li><strong>FastAPI 0.128.0</strong>: Modern async web framework with automatic API documentation</li>
<li><strong>LangGraph 0.2.0</strong>: Multi-agent orchestration framework for coordinating specialized agents</li>
<li><strong>LangChain 0.3.0</strong>: LLM integration layer with OpenAI GPT-4o-mini</li>
<li><strong>Jinja2 Templates</strong>: Server-side template rendering for dynamic HTML generation</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="frontend" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="frontend">Frontend</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>HTML5</strong>: Semantic markup with accessibility considerations</li>
<li><strong>CSS3</strong>: Custom lofi aesthetic with earthy color palette and block-style design</li>
<li><strong>Vanilla JavaScript</strong>: No frameworks; minimal dependencies for maximum control</li>
<li><strong>Chart.js 4.4.0</strong>: Progressive enhancement for data visualization</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="data-sources" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="data-sources">Data Sources</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Open-Meteo Marine API</strong>: Wave height, period, and direction (hourly &amp; daily aggregates)</li>
<li><strong>Open-Meteo Weather API</strong>: Wind speed and direction at 10m elevation</li>
<li><strong>OpenAI API</strong>: GPT-4o-mini for description generation and forecast synthesis</li>
</ul>
<hr>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="the-four-agent-pipeline" class="level1">
<h1>The Four-Agent Pipeline</h1>
<section id="agent-1-description-generator" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="agent-1-description-generator">Agent 1: Description Generator</h2>
